<div class="w-full bg-surface-container-lowest rounded-2xl rounded-tl-sm p-space-md shadow-sm space-y-space-md"><div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 pb-1"><div class="flex items-center gap-2"><div class="w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[18px]" style="font-variation-settings: 'FILL' 1;">auto_awesome</span></div><div><span class="inline-flex items-center px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-label-sm font-label-sm bg-primary/15 text-primary">Tutor Explanation</span></div></div><span class="font-code-sm text-code-sm text-outline">Confidence: 99.1%</span></div><div class="space-y-space-sm text-on-surface"><p class="font-body-md text-body-md text-on-surface leading-relaxed">In Operating Systems concurrency, a <strong>Mutex</strong> enforces strict thread ownership and mutual exclusion (binary state: 0 or 1), whereas a <strong>Counting Semaphore</strong> coordinates shared resource pools across arbitrary processes without ownership constraints:</p><div class="space-y-2"><div class="p-space-sm rounded-xl bg-surface-container-low flex gap-2.5 items-start"><div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-md bg-secondary text-on-secondary flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-label-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">1</div><div class="min-w-0"><h2 class="font-title-md text-title-md text-on-surface">Mutex Lock (Ownership Semantics)</h2><p class="font-body-md text-body-md text-on-surface-variant mt-0.5">Only the thread that acquired the lock (pthread_mutex_lock) can release it (pthread_mutex_unlock), preventing race conditions on critical sections.</p></div></div><div class="p-space-sm rounded-xl bg-surface-container-low flex gap-2.5 items-start"><div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-md bg-secondary text-on-secondary flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-label-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">2</div><div class="min-w-0"><h2 class="font-title-md text-title-md text-on-surface">Counting Semaphore (Signaling)</h2><p class="font-body-md text-body-md text-on-surface-variant mt-0.5">Initialized to integer N; sem_wait() decrements and blocks when 0, while sem_post() increments and unblocks any waiting thread without ownership check.</p></div></div><div class="p-space-sm rounded-xl bg-surface-container-low flex gap-2.5 items-start"><div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-md bg-secondary text-on-secondary flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-label-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">3</div><div class="min-w-0"><h2 class="font-title-md text-title-md text-on-surface">Coffman Deadlock Conditions</h2><p class="font-body-md text-body-md text-on-surface-variant mt-0.5">Deadlock occurs if all 4 hold simultaneously: (1) Mutual Exclusion, (2) Hold &amp; Wait, (3) No Preemption, and (4) Circular Wait.</p></div></div><div class="p-space-sm rounded-xl bg-surface-container-low flex gap-2.5 items-start"><div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-md bg-secondary text-on-secondary flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-label-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">4</div><div class="min-w-0"><h2 class="font-title-md text-title-md text-on-surface">Deadlock Prevention: Resource Ordering</h2><p class="font-body-md text-body-md text-on-surface-variant mt-0.5">Break circular wait by enforcing a strict global total ordering R_1 &lt; R_2 &lt; ... &lt; R_m. Every process must acquire resources strictly in increasing index sequence.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden bg-surface-container-highest"><div class="flex items-center justify-between px-space-sm py-1.5 bg-surface-container"><span class="font-code-sm text-code-sm text-on-surface-variant flex items-center gap-1"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[14px]">terminal</span>posix_semaphore_sync.c</span><button class="font-label-sm text-label-sm text-primary hover:underline flex items-center gap-0.5" id="copy-code-btn" type="button"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[14px]">content_copy</span><span>Copy</span></button></div><div class="p-space-sm overflow-x-auto text-on-surface-variant font-code-sm text-code-sm leading-relaxed"><div><span class="text-primary font-bold">sem_t</span> empty_slots, full_slots; // Producer-Consumer Sync</div><div class="pl-4 text-on-surface-variant/70">// Initialize with buffer capacity N = 10</div><div class="pl-4">sem_init(&amp;empty_slots, 0, 10); sem_init(&amp;full_slots, 0, 0);</div><div class="pl-4">sem_wait(&amp;empty_slots); // wait if buffer full</div><div class="pl-4">pthread_mutex_lock(&amp;buffer_mutex); // protect critical buffer</div><div class="pl-4">// Insert data into shared buffer...</div><div class="pl-4">pthread_mutex_unlock(&amp;buffer_mutex);</div><div>sem_post(&amp;full_slots); // notify consumer</div></div></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 pt-1"><button class="h-8 px-2.5 rounded-lg bg-surface-container text-on-surface-variant hover:text-on-surface flex items-center gap-1 font-label-sm text-label-sm transition-colors" id="action-copy" type="button"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]">content_copy</span><span>Copy Explanation</span></button><button class="h-8 px-2.5 rounded-lg bg-secondary-container/40 text-on-secondary-container hover:bg-secondary-container/60 flex items-center gap-1 font-label-sm text-label-sm transition-colors" id="action-flashcard" type="button"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]">style</span><span>Add to Flashcards</span></button><button class="h-8 px-2.5 rounded-lg bg-surface-container text-on-surface-variant hover:text-on-surface flex items-center gap-1 font-label-sm text-label-sm transition-colors" id="action-simpler" type="button"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]">psychology</span><span>Explain Simpler</span></button></div><div class="p-space-sm rounded-xl bg-surface-container-low space-y-2"><div class="flex items-center justify-between text-on-surface-variant"><span class="font-label-sm text-label-sm">Deadlock Prevention Matrix (Coffman Strategies)</spa